---
import PrivacyControls from "../components/PrivacyControls.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Vraj Patel"
  description="How vrajmpatel.com uses PostHog analytics and session replay by default, and how to opt out."
>
  <header class="max-w-3xl pb-10 sm:pb-14">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Site</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.035em] text-slate-950 dark:text-white sm:text-5xl">
      Privacy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
      This personal portfolio is a static site. Measurement is on by default.
      You can opt out of analytics and session replay independently, and
      the controls below are the only way to turn either one off.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-12 text-base leading-8 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 sm:text-lg">
    <PrivacyControls />

    <section aria-labelledby="choices-heading">
      <h2 id="choices-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950 dark:text-white">
        Your choices
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5">
        The controls on this page are the only way to opt out. There is no
        banner or first-visit prompt. Your choice is stored only in this
        browser and does not apply on other browsers or devices.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="analytics-heading">
      <h2 id="analytics-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950 dark:text-white">
        Analytics
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5">
        Unless you opt out, PostHog collects page views and page leaves to
        measure bounce rate and session duration, along with autocaptured
        interactions, heatmaps, web vitals, and dead clicks. Person profiles
        are configured as
        <code class="font-mono text-sm">identified_only</code>; this site does
        not call <code class="font-mono text-sm">identify()</code> or associate
        analytics with your name, account, or another direct identifier.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5">
        Referrer and UTM fields may be retained to show how visitors find the
        site. Current-page URLs exclude query strings and fragments, and ad
        click identifiers such as
        <code class="font-mono text-sm">gclid</code> and
        <code class="font-mono text-sm">fbclid</code> are discarded.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="replay-heading">
      <h2 id="replay-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950 dark:text-white">
        Session replay
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5">
        Unless you opt out, PostHog may record a masked replay of your visit.
        All form inputs—including email, password, and textarea fields—are
        masked. You may disable replay while keeping analytics on, or disable
        analytics while keeping replay on.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="storage-heading">
      <h2 id="storage-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950 dark:text-white">
        What is stored on this device
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5">
        Your analytics and replay choices are stored locally under
        <code class="font-mono text-sm">vrajmpatel-analytics-consent</code>.
        PostHog may also use first-party cookies or local storage for sessions
        and page-leave measurement. Your theme preference is stored separately
        and is not sent to PostHog.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="processor-heading">
      <h2 id="processor-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950 dark:text-white">
        Who processes the data
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5">
        PostHog processes events in its US Cloud service. The site includes a
        public project token, not a personal API key. GitHub Pages hosts the
        site. Events are sent to PostHog’s US endpoint unless a first-party
        ingestion proxy is configured.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
      <h2 id="contact-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950 dark:text-white">
        Questions
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5">
        To report a suspected privacy or security issue with this site, use
        <a
          href="https://github.com/basechildren/vrajmpatel.com/security/advisories/new"
          class="underline decoration-slate-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-blue-700 focus-visible:rounded-sm focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-600 dark:decoration-slate-700 dark:hover:text-blue-400"
        >
          GitHub private vulnerability reporting
        </a>.
        For general questions, use the
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/vrajmp/"
          class="underline decoration-slate-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-blue-700 focus-visible:rounded-sm focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-blue-600 dark:decoration-slate-700 dark:hover:text-blue-400"
        >
          LinkedIn profile
        </a>
        linked in the footer. This page is the portfolio’s privacy notice, not
        a terms-of-service agreement.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
